# modules/image/checks-langdeps.rules - the container-image module's own
# per-owner registry (rules/RULE-FORMAT.md §9's `checks-<name>.rules` row,
# docs/FOUNDATION.md tension 29) for IMG-11:
# language dependencies (npm/RubyGems/Composer/PyPI/Maven/Go) shipped inside
# the image rootfs, found by reusing the four existing `modules/sca/`
# tree-walkers against a bounded, declared extraction of this image's own
# conventional manifest locations.
#
# A SEPARATE FILE FROM checks-apk.rules/checks-dpkg.rules/checks-rpm.rules/
# checks-advisories.rules/checks-coverage.rules/checks-config.rules,
# per the binding "one registry per owner" rule and
# modules/image/checks-apk.rules' own identical precedent: this ticket's OWN
# file, never an append to a shared or sibling one a later ticket could then
# collide on.
#
# `script: langdeps.sh` for both records below - the whole ticket lives in
# ONE new driver file (modules/image/langdeps.sh), unlike apk/dpkg's
# enumerate-then-compare pair split across two tickets each.
#
# `tags: passive` - language-dependency extraction reads already-extracted
# local layer members with no network call and no mutation, mirroring every
# other image checks-*.rules file's own reasoning for the identical tag.
# Deliberately NO `tags: quick`: unlike a single-file parse plus one
# `db_lookup_exact` prefix test, this check's bounded extraction is
# `image_collect_metadata` over the whole IMAGE_LANGDEPS_DIRS x
# IMAGE_LANGDEPS_FILENAMES cross product (modules/image/langdeps.sh
# section 1) - still local-disk-only and still no network, but a real
# multiple of the cost every sibling image check pays, so it is not
# described as the cheapest coverage a run can buy.
#
# `coverage-scope: image-id` - the only legal value for the `IMAGE` module
# (rules/RULE-FORMAT.md §9.5.1's frozen table); the cell is the
# operator-declared stable id from `config/images.conf`, never the image
# digest or tag - a rebuild or retag must not reset coverage - and NEVER
# the `path-root` cell the reused `modules/sca/` walkers would otherwise set
# on their own raw findings; modules/image/langdeps.sh's own header explains
# the shadow-run re-emission that guarantees this.

id: IMAGE-LANGDEP-VULNERABLE_DEP-01
title: A language dependency (npm/RubyGems/Composer/PyPI/Maven/Go) pinned inside this image matches a known advisory
script: langdeps.sh
severity: high
confidence: high
cwe: CWE-1104
owasp: A06:2021
tags: passive
coverage-scope: image-id
remediation: Rebuild the image with the named dependency re-pinned to at
  least the advisory's fixed version (a lockfile edit and a fresh install,
  not a base-image bump - this is an application-level dependency, not an
  OS package) and re-scan.
references: CWE-1104

id: IMAGE-COV-LANGDEPS_NOT_SCANNED-01
title: Language-dependency scanning did NOT run inside this image - no advisory database, or no manifest found under any declared candidate location
script: langdeps.sh
severity: info
confidence: high
cwe: none
owasp: none
tags: passive
coverage-scope: image-id
remediation: Populate data/advisories.db for the affected ecosystem(s) with
  'tools/vendor-engines.sh advisories <ecosystem>' on a networked box (the
  no_advisories_db case), or confirm this image genuinely ships no
  package-lock.json/requirements.txt/go.mod/and-similar manifest at any of
  this module's declared conventional locations (the no_manifests_found
  case) - see this finding's own evidence for which reason applied.
